WEBVTT

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:04.400
A very important friend.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:17.340
Mr. Porte...

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:20.900
Couldn't sleep?

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:26.090
It's only natural for young people
to have a few sleepless nights.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.590
But you're not young anymore...

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:29.390
What did you say?

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:31.330
I'm sorry!

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:36.540
It's okay, it's okay. I really am an old man, after all.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.100
I'll help you with that.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:47.080
You're a much stronger girl than you realize.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.810
I'm not strong...

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:53.430
You just don't know you are.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:54.990
Mr. Porte...

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.810
The name of that transport ship, "Orion"...

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:01.460
I really liked it.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:06.040
It's taken from an old Earth myth.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:08.580
Oh, I know that one!

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:10.430
You know it?

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.650
Orion, who was stung by a scorpius and died...

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:18.180
...was placed in the sky by the gods at the request of his lover, Artemis.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:19.570
That's right.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:26.120
Even though they're far apart, Orion still watches over his beloved Artemis.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:30.850
I didn't think you were that romantic a person, Mr. Porte.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.330
Men are all romantics!

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:39.250
Mr. Porte! Sharla!

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:40.880
Good morning!

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:42.810
Good morning, everyone.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.290
You could have woken us up.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.820
At this rate, we'll be done by the end of the day.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:49.730
Really?

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:54.490
Okay, in that case let's start loading the luggage.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:00.190
This tank has our water, so don't drop it.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.410
My arms...

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:05.880
This is the last of it.

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:09.700
Pague, thank you!

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:18.700
We have about two weeks' worth of food?

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:23.630
Yes, because according to Chako's data we should reach the mainland in about ten days.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:26.100
With this much, we'll have some to spare.

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:30.230
Oh, its done?

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:33.880
It's great!

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.070
I'm definitely on top!

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.610
As you please.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:41.000
Maybe Howard should be on the bottom.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:44.100
Since Howard has bad sleeping posture.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.530
What did you say?

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.280
Honestly, what a rude lot!

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:54.640
It's okay here.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.110
What is it?

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:05.120
Contrary to your appearance, you're quite exceptional.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:08.370
Are you praisin' me or insultin' me?

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.070
What's up with gramps?

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.550
What a weird guy.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.110
Bell!

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.590
Should I help?

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:21.810
No, I'm fine on my own.

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:23.260
Oh, really.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:30.750
I don't know how many times your strength and kindness have saved everyone.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.490
Keep up the good work!

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:38.760
Hey, Kaoru.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:42.000
What are those?

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.430
Fishing rods, just in case.

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:46.900
That's a good idea.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:47.610
Thanks.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:51.370
You're cool, stylish, and handsome.

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:55.080
Just like me in my younger days.

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:58.640
From now on, you'll become an even better man!

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:01.310
I guarantee it!

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:10.860
Hey!

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:13.900
Why are you slacking off?

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:17.830
You're wrong! I was about to get to work!

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:21.850
At first I thought you were a helpless spoiled whiner...

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:24.840
...but I can't stay mad at you.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:30.450
When you're around, I smile, and when I smile, I cheer up.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:34.550
Just don't overdo it. Keep it in moderation.

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:36.570
What?

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:38.770
Nice work.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.210
We'll be finished loading in just a little while.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:43.610
Really.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:48.110
I hope you can meet your mother and father.

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:51.380
Thanks! I'll go feed Pague.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:55.430
Mr. Porte, are your injuries okay yet?

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.910
I'm good as new.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:00.240
But please rest a little.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.430
You're wise and courageous.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:06.190
Everyone relies on you.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:08.440
But...

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:12.290
Nobody will begrudge you if you loosen up once in a while.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:18.670
We're finally going to leave this island soon.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:21.230
As expected, you're nervous as well?

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:22.660
Mr. Porte!

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.190
You don't have to bear it alone.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:27.150
You have friends.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:28.150
Yes.

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:34.840
In their entire life, not everyone has what you'd call true friendship.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:38.830
And yet, you've all found it in your youth.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:40.110
Yes.

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:44.160
Just that is reason enough to have been born.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.750
You're our friend too, Mr. Porte.

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:48.630
I am?

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:49.680
Yes.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:51.620
A very important friend.

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:53.210
Thank you.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:59.420
I believe you'll make it back to your colony safely.

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:02.330
No, you'll definitely make it!

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:20.410
Just a lil' more!

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:24.060
Put your hips into it!

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:34.740
We did it!

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:37.840
A fine piece of work.

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:40.350
Sharla, give it a name!

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:42.170
Me?

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:43.850
Sharla, please.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:49.440
Let me think about it.

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:52.340
Don't be stuck up about it!

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:56.640
But it's because I want to give it a wonderful name.

00:08:57.130 --> 00:09:00.000
What's the problem? We'll just hafta look forward to it.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:14.380
We're here.

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:18.340
Of course we'd want to spend our last night here at Everyone's House.

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:19.540
Exactly.

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:40.220
It's time to say farewell to this island.

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:42.610
Now that the time has come, it's somehow lonely.

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:46.570
If you want, you can stay behind on your own.

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:47.710
No way!

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:56.540
But so many things have happened.

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:51.880
So many things happened, but now they're just good memories.

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:56.500
Thanks to Howard, we were sure not to be bored.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.230
What did you say?

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:01.340
Honestly, you lot never quiet down!

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:03.450
Shut up!

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:18.830
I almost can't believe it.

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:22.240
How we did all of this just by ourselves.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:26.170
We even built this house together.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:32.410
We've all done well.

00:12:52.490 --> 00:12:54.600
Not yet!

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:57.900
Honestly!

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:05.310
Mr. Porte?

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:06.560
Hey.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.500
What's wrong? Can't sleep?

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:11.200
For some reason I'm wide awake.

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:13.080
We'll be at sea starting tomorrow.

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:15.670
You should sleep a little.

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:19.010
Well, will you come over here for a minute and sit down?

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:21.650
Okay.

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:23.880
Is everyone asleep?

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:29.320
It's because they all worked so hard. They must be exhausted.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.280
At sea starting tomorrow, huh...

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:36.120
It's thanks to you that we can leave this island, Mr. Porte.

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:39.170
No, that was your hard work.

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:42.840
I couldn't have done it if you weren't here.

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:45.660
I'm really glad to have met you.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:49.170
I'm happy to have met all of you as well.

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:51.790
And we'll be counting on you from now on as well.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:57.230
I wish I could have talked to my son like this...

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:04.750
This is...

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:09.640
You're now a proper mechanic.

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:14.600
Although it'll take a lot more training before you're as good as me.

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:18.360
Thank you, Mr. Porte.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.210
I'm tired.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.000
Maybe I'll try to get some rest.

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:26.160
Right here? You'll catch a cold!

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.190
You try it too, Shingo.

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:30.690
The night wind feels great.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:37.560
When you close your eyes, it feels like you're drifting slowly through space.

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:44.330
It's true. It feels great.

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:47.550
You're all the best.

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:50.370
The best of friends.

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:56.780
Some day when I become a mechanic, I'd like to travel on the same ship as you, Mr. Porte.

00:14:57.720 --> 00:15:00.880
I'd like to see Titan or Upsilon.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:05.580
I'll do my best to become a first-class mechanic.

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:09.740
And then we can travel all over space together.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:15.040
Mr. Porte?

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:17.830
Oh, he's asleep.

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:22.070
Good night.

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:52.520
Looks like it was space sickness.

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:55.480
Why didn't he tell us?

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:58.360
Because he didn't want to worry us.

00:15:58.550 --> 00:16:02.060
Until the very end, he was worried about us.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:03.370
That's right.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:09.040
Rest... in peace.

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:12.940
Hey, can we not see Mr. Porte again?

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:14.450
Adam...

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.180
Mr. Porte is...

00:16:20.090 --> 00:16:21.140
We'll see him.

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:23.930
Mr. Porte has become a star.

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:27.980
So he'll always be watching over us.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:30.030
Sharla...

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:32.300
Isn't that right, Mr. Porte?

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:35.780
Just like Orion watching over Artemis.

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:39.540
That's right. If we don't keep our heads, we'll get bogged down again.

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:48.310
I think the name for this ship should be The Orion, like the transport ship Mr. Porte was on.

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:51.160
Mr. Porte liked it a lot.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:53.070
The Orion...

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:56.370
I agree. It's great.

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:00.870
It's about time we departed.

00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:02.440
Shingo, let's go.

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:08.870
Mr. Porte...

00:17:09.640 --> 00:17:10.730
Off we go.

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:13.430
Please watch over us.

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:36.810
Shingo!

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:41.370
Mr. Porte, I'll definitely become a proper mechanic!

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:45.500
And some day I'll tell your son...

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:50.090
...that you were the best mechanic in the universe!

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:54.130
Thank you...

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:57.380
...for everything.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:04.180
Shingo...

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:16.430
Huh? Where's Adam?

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:18.910
Come to think of it, I haven't seen him for a while.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:20.820
He's saying his farewells.

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:22.500
Farewells?

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:27.310
I'm going on a trip.

00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:30.160
I'm with friends, so I'll be fine.

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:32.240
Don't worry.

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.200
Goodbye.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:45.570
This is great! I'm getting excited!

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:47.700
Howard's going to pilot it?

00:18:47.990 --> 00:18:51.120
Yeah, the first part is critical!

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:53.630
Shouldn't Shingo be first?

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:56.650
He knows the most about the system, after all.

00:18:56.850 --> 00:18:59.760
It's fine! Leave it to me!

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:01.520
Everyone's life rests on this.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:02.930
Think it over.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:11.740
I've no choice!

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:13.800
I'll just have to hand this over to Shingo.

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:15.300
Keep your wits about you.

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:20.630
All ready over here.

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:22.130
Alright, here we go.

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:23.890
Everyone hold on tight.

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:25.580
Solar system on!

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:30.860
Energy output: 20%.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:33.000
30... 40...

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:35.180
Gravity control unit on.

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:44.740
All engines ready. System all green.

00:19:45.340 --> 00:19:46.950
Energy output stable.

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:47.930
Roger.

00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:50.330
Activating gravity control unit.

00:19:50.510 --> 00:19:51.340
Lifting off!

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:07.840
It stopped.

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:09.000
Shingo...

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:10.990
It's okay, it'll work.

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:15.040
It's the ship Mr. Porte and I built. It'll definitely work.

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:18.040
Work...

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:20.660
Work!

00:20:24.980 --> 00:20:26.630
Gravity Control Unit active!

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:30.260
Shingo!

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:32.360
Mr. Porte...

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:35.290
Orion: launch!

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:09.640
Thanks, Kaoru.

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:11.590
Are you okay, Shingo?

00:21:11.590 --> 00:21:14.250
Yeah. Let's go full sail toward the sea!

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:39.300
Everyone, hold on tight!

00:22:26.060 --> 00:22:27.980
You did it, Shingo!

00:22:34.390 --> 00:22:35.700
We made it...

00:22:38.140 --> 00:22:39.000
It's Pague!

00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:40.730
Pague!

00:22:40.730 --> 00:22:42.000
Goodbye!

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:43.390
Thank you!

00:22:52.130 --> 00:22:55.650
Alright everyone, let's head for the mainland!

00:23:03.450 --> 00:23:06.900
We've started our voyage to the mainland...

00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:11.060
Everyone's seasick and sayin' they wanna go back to the island.

00:23:11.060 --> 00:23:13.760
No way! We can't go back at this point!

00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:19.160
But putting everyone through such hardship to go to the mainland...

00:23:19.610 --> 00:23:21.380
Luna, chin up!

00:23:21.560 --> 00:23:24.340
Once you've decided, all you can do is believe in yourself and follow through!

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:29.550
Next time: Don't complain
